# Cloudflare Pages redirects. First match wins; the trailing number is the status served.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-09-03, measured against production with curl, not assumed).
# Cloudflare Pages deploys this repository as it stands, so every file in it is a URL. That
# was never a decision anybody made, and it meant the engineering handoffs at the root were
# public documents:
#
#   /HANDOFF_the-day-the-site-went-live_2026-09-02.md   200   12558 bytes
#   /CONTENT_PRESSURE_TEST_2026-08-23.md                200   45807 bytes
#   /README.md                                          200    4768 bytes
#   /check.sh                                           200   22474 bytes
#   /check-site.py                                      200
#   /tools/es_strings.py                                200
#
# A handoff is an internal document. It quotes the CEO, names the deploy topology and the
# rollback command, records what is owed and what was got wrong, and says which defects
# reached TestFlight users. None of that is a page of this website.
#
# 🔒 THE FAILURE MODE HERE IS PUBLICATION, AND PUBLICATION IS THE ONE THING YOU CANNOT UNDO.
# Anything served at 200 can already be cached, archived or indexed, so this file stops the
# bleeding and does not repair the past. Treat everything above as already public.
#
# SCOPE, AND WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. This blocks internal documents and the gate
# programs. It does NOT touch /record/anchors.json, which is published data the record page
# is built from and is meant to be readable, and it does not touch anything under /assets/.
#
# The stronger fix is a Cloudflare Pages BUILD OUTPUT DIRECTORY holding only the deployable
# files, so a new internal document cannot become a URL by being saved in the wrong folder.
# That is a change in the Cloudflare dashboard rather than in this repository, so it is the
# CEO's to make, and this file is what protects the site until he does.
#
# To publish any of these deliberately, delete its line. That is the whole revert.

/HANDOFF_*                 /404.html  404
/CONTENT_PRESSURE_TEST_*   /404.html  404
/README.md                 /404.html  404
/check.sh                  /404.html  404
/check-site.py             /404.html  404
/stamp-assets.py           /404.html  404
/tools/*                   /404.html  404
